# Metadata management workflow

`pebbles metadata set <id> <key> <value>` upserts one metadata field on an
issue; `pebbles metadata unset <id> <key>` removes one (a no-op when
absent); `pebbles metadata get <id> [<key>]` prints all pairs or a single
value. `pebbles list --metadata <key>=<value>` filters by metadata
(repeatable, AND) and composes with --status, --issue-type, --search, and
--tag. Keys and values are trimmed on entry; keys must be non-empty, values
may be empty; matching is exact and case-sensitive.

Fixture store: 111 (Login button..., todo bug), 222 (JWT token
authentication system, todo design), 333 (User can login..., in progress
usecase), 444 (Export users to CSV, done usecase). All without metadata
initially.

## Baseline list (updated_at descending)

```console
$ pebbles list
111 [bug] [TODO] Login button doesn't respond on mobile ✓
222 [des] [TODO] JWT token authentication system ✓
333 [uc] [IN PROGRESS] User can login with email and password ✓
444 [uc] [DONE] Export users to CSV

```
